Annotations: |
  `Backtesting` is the simulation engine: it replays historical OHLCV data through an
  `IStrategy`'s lifecycle hooks exactly as the live bot would call them, producing the same
  `Trade`/`LocalTrade` records a live run would, without touching a real exchange. It composes
  nearly every other documented cell, so it sits at the root of the spine.

  Uses `ExchangeResolver` and `StrategyResolver` to build a missing `Exchange`/`IStrategy` when
  one isn't supplied by the caller, and internally owns a `PairListManager`, a
  `ProtectionManager`, and a `DataProvider` — the same kind of objects the live bot would use —
  so strategy code sees an identical runtime environment in backtest and live modes.

---

"Backtesting(config: dict[str, Any], exchange: Exchange | None, progress_callback: Any | None)":
  location: backtesting.py
  annotations: |
    `exchange`: reused live-mode-style `Exchange` for OHLCV loading only; built internally via
    ExchangeResolver.load_exchange when omitted
    `progress_callback`: optional hook invoked periodically to report backtest progress
  methods:
    "start()": |
      Run a full backtest end-to-end: load data, run the strategy, print/store results.

      Algorithm:
      1. load_bt_data to get OHLCV data and the effective TimeRange
      2. backtest_one_strategy for each strategy under test
      3. Hand results to the optimize-reports subsystem for display/storage
    "backtest(processed: dict[str, DataFrame], start_date: datetime, end_date: datetime) -> results:dict[str, Any]": |
      Core per-candle simulation loop over `processed` data between `start_date`/`end_date`,
      calling the strategy's lifecycle hooks and recording resulting `LocalTrade`s.

      Constraints:
      - Performance-critical: called once per strategy per backtest, and repeatedly (once per
        hyperopt epoch) when driven by the hyperopt engine
    "backtest_one_strategy(strat: IStrategy, data: dict[str, DataFrame], timerange: Any)": |
      Prepare one strategy (load its HyperStrategyMixin parameters, run populate_indicators/
      populate_entry_trend/populate_exit_trend over `data`) and invoke backtest for it.
    "load_bt_data() -> result:tuple[dict[str, DataFrame], Any]": |
      Load historical OHLCV data for the configured pairs/timeframe/timerange.

      `result`: (data, timerange)
    "init_backtest()": |
      Reset per-run state (wallets, progress tracker) before a strategy's backtest starts.
    "reset_backtest(enable_protections: bool)": |
      Clear trades/locks/custom-data between successive strategy or hyperopt-epoch runs.

      `enable_protections`: re-run `ProtectionManager` checks during this reset

"get_strategy_run_id(strategy: IStrategy) -> run_id:str":
  location: backtest_caching.py
  annotations: |
    Compute a stable hash identifying this exact combination of strategy code, parameters, and
    config, used to detect when a cached backtest result can be reused.

"get_backtest_metadata_filename(filename: str) -> path:str":
  location: backtest_caching.py
  annotations: |
    Derive the .meta.json sidecar path that stores metadata for a backtest results file.

